From c362c74ae98743b8bbab5e74da6d2ab34a17c7e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:40:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 extension tab groups: tabs.group and tabGroups for
 registry tabs, tab events, window focus

Claude in Chrome anchors its session in a tab group: it groups the side
panel's tab with tabs.group and names it with tabGroups.update. Registry tabs
have no TabStripModel, so both failed and every browser action reported
"anchor tab group not established".

Tab groups now live in the bridge, next to the logical extension windows:
tabs.group (new group, or an existing one) and ungroup, tabGroups.get,
query, update and move (in place only), the tabs groupId field and the
tabs.query groupId filter, and the tabGroups onCreated, onUpdated and
onRemoved events with tabs.onUpdated {groupId}. A group stays in one
window: grouping a tab from another window is an error, since the host owns
placement. A tab that leaves its window or the host's mapping leaves its
group; the last tab out removes the group. Colours follow Chromium's order
of unused colours. The host shows grouped tabs as ordinary tabs.

Mapped tabs now send tabs.onCreated, onActivated, onRemoved and onUpdated
(status on commit and on the first stop after it, url, title, mutedInfo),
after TabsEventRouter::TabEntry; each listener's tab is looked up by ID at
dispatch. windows.update focuses a window through the host's activation
request (geometry and state are errors); windows.create accepts the popup
type and ignores its geometry (the host opens a Little Arc); chrome://newtab
in tabs.create and windows.create is the host's blank tab.

ABI 1.50 extension_tab_groups, no new functions or structs. Bridge 0.53.0.

Last rebased: 2026-11-08 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
